  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Winterization Support for Conflict-Affected Populations in Ukraine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM identified solid fuel support as the second most pressing need expressed by respondents in Ukraine during the past winter. Overall, 24 per cent of non-displaced, 23 per cent of internally displaced persons (IDPs) and 18 per cent of returnees indicated that they required such support. The numbers are similar for support with heating appliances at 18 per cent, 27 per cent and 18 per cent respectively (General Population Survey Round 12). 
 
Through this intervention, IOM contributes to addressing urgent winterization needs of conflict-affected populations in Donetsk and Kharkiv oblasts while empowering local partners by building their capacity.  In line with the priority activities identified in the OCHA Ukraine Winter Response Plan 2023-2024 and the Allocation Strategy, the project supports vulnerable and conflict-affected individuals to cope with the harsh weather during the 2023-2024 winter. To deliver these results, IOM is working in partnership with active local partners.</narrative>
  </description>
